Feature: The six buttons of the radio
  The six buttons on the front of the radio are the six flight modes that the plane needs.
  Press the button for the mode that you want:

  1. QHOVER: a hover. The throttle stick sets the climb. The plane drifts with the wind.
  2. QLOITER: a hover that holds the plane at one place. Use it to take off and land.
  3. FBWA: forward flight that levels itself. The sticks set the angle of bank and pitch.
  4. CRUISE: forward flight that holds the height and the heading. Use it to travel.
  5. AUTO: the plane flies the [[mission]] on the vehicle.
  6. QRTL: the plane flies to [[home]] and lands there, straight down and softly.

  [[The throttle stick in a hover]] shows QLOITER, [[Forward flight with self-levelling]] shows
  FBWA and [[Switches]] shows the buttons. Mission flights in AUTO are in [[Flying a mission]].

  Expectation: QHOVER is a hover mode
    Given the vehicle is armed
    And the flight is hovering
    And the height above home is at least 15 m
    And the throttle stick is high
    When the pilot switches to QHOVER
    Then the autopilot mode is QHOVER
    And the flight is hovering

  Expectation: CRUISE changes a hover into forward flight with the radio
    Given the vehicle is armed
    And the flight is hovering
    And the height above home is at least 15 m
    And the throttle stick is high
    When the pilot switches to cruise
    Then the flight is cruising
    And the autopilot mode is CRUISE

  Expectation: QRTL brings the plane home and lands it softly
  A soft landing is one at less than 2 m/s.
    Given the vehicle is armed
    And the plane is flying
    When the pilot sends the plane home
    Then the autopilot mode is QRTL
    And the plane is on the ground
    And the last landing is soft
